  "content": {
    "id": "v2-a6564-p25-practice-slot-6-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Find the domain of $f(g(x))$ for each pair of functions.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "v2-a6564-p25-practice-slot-6-slot6-q-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=\\sqrt{x^2-16}$ and $g(x)=x+2$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x\\le-6$ or $x\\ge2$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}f(g(x))&=\\sqrt{(x+2)^2-16}\\\\f(g(x))&=\\sqrt{(x+2-4)(x+2+4)}\\\\f(g(x))&=\\sqrt{(x-2)(x+6)}\\end{aligned}$$\nThe radicand must be non-negative:\n$$(x-2)(x+6)\\ge0$$\nThe product is non-negative outside the roots, including the endpoints. Hence the domain is $x\\le-6$ or $x\\ge2$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 45
      },
      {
        "id": "v2-a6564-p25-practice-slot-6-slot6-q-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=\\sqrt{x^2-4}$ and $g(x)=x-3$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x\\le1$ or $x\\ge5$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}f(g(x))&=\\sqrt{(x-3)^2-4}\\\\f(g(x))&=\\sqrt{(x-3-2)(x-3+2)}\\\\f(g(x))&=\\sqrt{(x-5)(x-1)}\\end{aligned}$$\nThe radicand must be non-negative:\n$$(x-5)(x-1)\\ge0$$\nThe product is non-negative outside the roots, including the endpoints. Hence the domain is $x\\le1$ or $x\\ge5$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 45
      }
    ]
  },
